# SecAgent (on-demand pi harness — MR review, code analysis, testgen, docs) — Fedora/FIPS.
# secdeploy installs SecAgent as a harness, NOT a standing service: there is no chat bridge and
# no systemd unit. Copy to /etc/secsuite/secagent.env and fill in the secret below. secdeploy
# seeds this file once (`test -f ... || install ...`) and never overwrites an existing one.
#
# Structured audit log (CMMC AU controls) — under this component's writable state dir
# (/var/lib/secsuite/secagent). Fixed, not topology-derived.
SECAGENT_AUDIT__PATH=/var/lib/secsuite/secagent/audit/audit.jsonl
#
# SecSSO service-account client secret (client_credentials, headless service identity —
# "svc-secagent"), used by `secagent token` for non-interactive (CI / MCP) runs. The value is
# the COMPOSITE base64("svc-secagent:" + SecSSO's SECAGENT_SVC_APP_PASSWORD) — Authentik's
# creds-path grant, which makes the issued token's sub exactly "svc-secagent" (see
# secsso/blueprints/secagent-service.yaml). Run `./bootstrap/secsso.sh secagent-config` on the
# SecSSO host and paste the printed value here (secdeploy has no cross-host way to fetch it —
# see docs/fedora-fips.md#secagent-the-pi-harness). For interactive use, `secagent login`
# (device-code) needs no secret here at all.
SECAGENT_CLIENT_SECRET=
